IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tfm-dates`

-- Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912 (Tas) -- the rules a person who claims provision out of a deceased person's
-- estate meets, and those a beneficiary of the estate meets in answering the claim: who may apply (ss 2, 3A), the
-- Court's power to order provision and its forms (s 3), applications on another's behalf (s 3(4), (5)), the summons and
-- its service (s 4), the net estate (s 7(a)), refusal for character or conduct (s 8(1)), the spouse's provision on
-- remarriage (s 9(4)), rescinding or altering an order (s 9(5), (5A), (6)), who bears the provision (s 10A), and the
-- time limit and its extension (s 11).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in tfm-seat.l4 (the claimant) and tfm-seat-beneficiary.l4 (the
-- beneficiary), which IMPORT it and never restate a rule. Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" definition, an "if"
-- or "where" condition that fails, "unless", "shall not", "shall have no jurisdiction"); or NOTHING where the Act does
-- not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments the Act leaves to the Court or a judge
-- ("without adequate provision for his proper maintenance and support", "in the opinion of the Court ... should
-- disentitle", "if in the opinion of the Court ... it is desirable") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them,
-- never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is yes` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST b THEN b
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is no` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST b THEN (NOT b)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 2, 3A -- who may apply`

-- s 3A: "An application under subsection (1) of section three for provision out of the estate of a deceased person may
-- be made by or on behalf of all or any of the following persons, that is to say: (a) The spouse of the deceased person;
-- (b) The children of the deceased person; (c) The parents of the deceased person, if the deceased person dies without
-- leaving a spouse or any children; (d) A person whose marriage to the deceased person has been dissolved or annulled
-- and who at the date of the death of the deceased person was receiving or entitled to receive maintenance from the
-- deceased person whether pursuant to an order of a court, or to an agreement or otherwise; and (e) A person whose
-- significant relationship, within the meaning of the Relationships Act 2003, with the deceased person had ceased before
-- the date of the death ... and who was receiving or entitled to receive maintenance from the deceased person ...".
--
-- s 2(1): "child includes -- (a) an adopted child; and (b) a stepchild; and (c) a surrogate child"; "spouse includes the
-- person with whom a person is, or was at the time of his or her death, in a significant relationship, within the
-- meaning of the Relationships Act 2003"; "stepchild means, in relation to a person -- (a) a child of that person's
-- spouse; and (b) a child whose natural parent was the spouse of that person at the time of the natural parent's death";
-- "surrogate child" (a child by virtue of s 26(1) of the Surrogacy Act 2012 or a corresponding law). "Spouse" (beyond
-- the inclusion), "child", "adopted", "significant relationship" and the Surrogacy Act status are borrowed or undefined:
-- each is asked as a fact by the choice of relationship.
DECLARE `Relationship to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `spouse by marriage`
    `partner in a significant relationship at the death`
    `child`
    `adopted child`
    `child of the deceased's spouse`
    `child whose natural parent was the deceased's spouse when that parent died`
    `surrogate child`
    `parent`
    `former spouse, the marriage dissolved or annulled`
    `former partner, the significant relationship ended before the death`
    `another relationship`

-- s 2(2): the stepchild definition "as substituted by the Justice and Related Legislation (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act
-- 2015, does not apply in respect of a claim against the estate of a person whose death occurred before the
-- commencement of that Act". The history note dates the substitution "Applied:13 Oct 2015", taken as the commencement
-- (fork F2).
`s 2(2) -- the day the stepchild definition commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 13 10 2015

GIVEN `my relationship` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) -- I am a stepchild by the definition` `my relationship` IF
        `my relationship` EQUALS `child of the deceased's spouse`
    OR  `my relationship` EQUALS `child whose natural parent was the deceased's spouse when that parent died`

-- Whether I am a person by whom or on whose behalf an application may be made.
-- * spouse by marriage, a partner in a significant relationship at the death ("spouse includes"), a child, an adopted
--   child, a surrogate child ("child includes"): JUST TRUE.
-- * a stepchild by the 2015 definition: JUST TRUE for a death on or after 13 October 2015; for an earlier death, NOTHING
--   (NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources -- the earlier definition is not in the consolidation).
-- * a parent: "if the deceased person dies without leaving a spouse or any children": JUST FALSE when the deceased left
--   one (an "if" that fails).
-- * a former spouse or former partner: JUST TRUE if receiving or entitled to receive maintenance from the deceased at
--   the date of death; otherwise NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: a limit in the text's own wording with no "only"; fork F3).
-- * anyone else (a grandchild, a brother or sister, another dependant): NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: s 3A lists without
--   closing the list with "only"; fork F3, the other reading being JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `my relationship` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
      `the deceased left a spouse or any children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was receiving or entitled to receive maintenance from the deceased at the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3A -- I may apply for provision` `my relationship` `the deceased left a spouse or any children` `I was receiving or entitled to receive maintenance from the deceased at the death` `the day of the death` MEANS
    IF `s 2(1) -- I am a stepchild by the definition` `my relationship`
    THEN IF `the days from` `s 2(2) -- the day the stepchild definition commenced` `to` `the day of the death` AT LEAST 0
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `my relationship`
         WHEN `spouse by marriage` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `partner in a significant relationship at the death` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `child` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `adopted child` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `surrogate child` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `parent` THEN
             IF `the deceased left a spouse or any children`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE JUST TRUE
         WHEN `former spouse, the marriage dissolved or annulled` THEN
             IF `I was receiving or entitled to receive maintenance from the deceased at the death`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `former partner, the significant relationship ended before the death` THEN
             IF `I was receiving or entitled to receive maintenance from the deceased at the death`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `my relationship` IS A `Relationship to the deceased`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(4) -- I am the spouse` `my relationship` IF
        `my relationship` EQUALS `spouse by marriage`
    OR  `my relationship` EQUALS `partner in a significant relationship at the death`

§§ `s 11 -- the time to take out the summons`

-- s 11(1): "Except as provided by subsection (2) of this section, the Court or judge shall have no jurisdiction to hear
-- any application, or to make any order under this Act, unless the summons hereinbefore mentioned [the s 4 summons in
-- chambers] be taken out before or not later than three months after the date of grant of probate of the will of the
-- deceased person, or letters of administration of the estate of the deceased person, as the case may be."
--
-- The regulative rule: from the grant, the applicant must take out the summons within the days to the corresponding day
-- three months later (fork F1; a summons on that last day is in time). It starts at the grant (time 0), so a summons on
-- day n after the grant is at time n. A summons before the grant needs no trace: "before" the grant is in time. It takes
-- a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `take out the summons`

GIVEN `the days of the three months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 11(1) -- the three months after the grant` `the days of the three months` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `take out the summons`
    WITHIN `the days of the three months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "the summons was not taken out before or within three months after the grant of probate or letters of administration, so the Court has no jurisdiction unless it extends the time (s 11(1), (2))"

GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 11(1) -- the last day for the summons` `the day of the grant` MEANS `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` `the day of the grant`

GIVEN `the day of the summons` IS A DATE, `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the summons on` `the day of the summons` `is in time after the grant on` `the day of the grant` IF
    IF `the time of the summons` AT MOST 0
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 11(1) -- the three months after the grant` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `take out the summons` `the time of the summons`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` (`s 11(1) -- the last day for the summons` `the day of the grant`)
        `the time of the summons` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` `the day of the summons`

-- Whether the Court has jurisdiction to hear my application, on the day my summons is taken out.
-- * s 3(4): where the Court has ordered another person's application to be regarded as made on behalf of all persons
--   entitled, it is "for the purposes of section eleven ... treated as an application made by all of those persons"; if
--   that summons was in time, so is mine: JUST TRUE.
-- * no grant yet: "before" the grant is in time: JUST TRUE.
-- * a summons in the three months (the trace FULFILLED): JUST TRUE.
-- * s 11(2): the Court has extended the time to a day on or after my summons: JUST TRUE.
-- * otherwise: "shall have no jurisdiction ... unless": JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `a grant has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `the day of the summons` IS A DATE
      `another's in-time application is treated as made by all entitled persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the extended time` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11 -- the Court has jurisdiction to hear my application` `a grant has been made` `the day of the grant` `the day of the summons` `another's in-time application is treated as made by all entitled persons` `the Court has extended the time` `the last day of the extended time` MEANS
    IF `another's in-time application is treated as made by all entitled persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF NOT `a grant has been made`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the summons on` `the day of the summons` `is in time after the grant on` `the day of the grant`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF `the Court has extended the time` AND `the days from` `the day of the summons` `to` `the last day of the extended time` AT LEAST 0
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Summons deadline` IS ONE OF
    `the three months have not begun: you may take out your summons now, and at the latest three months after the grant of probate or letters of administration`
    `take out your summons by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `a grant has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Summons deadline`
`s 11(1) -- by when I must take out the summons` `a grant has been made` `the day of the grant` MEANS
    IF `a grant has been made`
    THEN `take out your summons by` (`s 11(1) -- the last day for the summons` `the day of the grant`)
    ELSE `the three months have not begun: you may take out your summons now, and at the latest three months after the grant of probate or letters of administration`

-- s 11(2): "upon application being made in that behalf by a person claiming the benefit of this Act, the Court or a
-- judge may ... extend the time ... for such further period as the Court or judge may think necessary"; (3): even
-- "notwithstanding that the time ... may have expired"; (4): "An application under subsection (2) ... shall be made
-- before the final distribution of the estate". Whether I may apply for an extension: JUST FALSE once the estate has
-- been finally distributed (a period the text fixes in its own words: "before"); JUST TRUE otherwise, whether or not
-- the three months have expired. Whether the Court grants it is its discretion, not answered.
GIVEN `the estate has been finally distributed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2)-(4) -- I may apply for an extension of time` `the estate has been finally distributed` MEANS
    IF `the estate has been finally distributed`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 3(1) -- the Court may order provision`

-- s 3(1): "If a person dies, whether testate or intestate, and in terms of his will or as a result of his intestacy any
-- person by whom or on whose behalf application ... may be made under this Act is left without adequate provision for
-- his proper maintenance and support thereafter, the Court or a judge may, in its or his discretion, on application ...
-- order that such provision as the Court or judge ... thinks proper shall be made out of the estate". Whether I was left
-- without adequate provision for my proper maintenance and support is the Court's judgment, asked as a fact. JUST TRUE
-- means the Court MAY order provision (it remains a discretion, s 3(1), and s 8(1) may lead it to refuse). An "if"
-- that fails, a parent excluded by s 3A(c), or no jurisdiction under s 11: JUST FALSE. Standing NOTHING (s 3A): NOTHING.
GIVEN `I may apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Court has jurisdiction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `I was left without adequate provision for my proper maintenance and support` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) -- the Court may order provision for me` `I may apply` `the Court has jurisdiction` `I was left without adequate provision for my proper maintenance and support` MEANS
    IF `it is no` `I may apply`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it is no` `the Court has jurisdiction`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF NOT `I was left without adequate provision for my proper maintenance and support`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `it is yes` `I may apply` AND `it is yes` `the Court has jurisdiction`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING

-- s 8(1): "The Court or judge may refuse any such application if the character or conduct of any person by or on behalf
-- of whom the application is made is such as in the opinion of the Court or judge should disentitle him or her to the
-- benefit of any provision under this Act." The opinion is the Court's, asked as a fact. An "if" that fails: JUST
-- FALSE (s 8(1) gives no ground to refuse on these facts; the Court's s 3(1) discretion remains).
GIVEN `the Court is of the opinion my character or conduct should disentitle me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) -- the Court may refuse for character or conduct` `the Court is of the opinion my character or conduct should disentitle me` MEANS
    IF `the Court is of the opinion my character or conduct should disentitle me`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 3(2), (3) -- the forms of provision`

-- s 3(2): "the Court or judge may order that the provision ... shall consist of -- (a) the payment to the applicant of a
-- lump sum; (b) a life interest or any lesser interest in any dwelling-house belonging to that estate; or (c) a life
-- interest or any lesser interest in a dwelling-house that the Court or judge may order to be purchased for occupation by
-- the applicant"; (3): for (c) estate moneys may be spent buying the fee simple "notwithstanding any provision or
-- direction to the contrary in the will". s 3(2) is "In addition to, and without prejudice to," s 3(1)'s general power:
-- another form is not excluded, and s 3(2) does not name it (NOTHING-kind: the text lists without closing the list;
-- s 3(1)'s "such provision as ... thinks proper" may reach it: fork F4).
DECLARE `Form of provision` IS ONE OF
    `a lump sum`
    `a life interest or lesser interest in a dwelling-house of the estate`
    `a life interest or lesser interest in a dwelling-house bought for me to live in`
    `another form`

GIVEN `the form` IS A `Form of provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2) -- the provision may take this form` `the form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `another form` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 3(5) -- an application by the executor on my behalf`

-- s 3(5): "The executor or administrator ..., on behalf of a person who is entitled to make an application under
-- subsection (1) ... and who is not of full age or mental capacity, may -- (a) make an application under that
-- subsection; or (b) apply to the Court or a judge for directions as to whether he should make an application". Not of
-- full age or mental capacity is asked as a fact. The person must be entitled to apply (s 3A): its answer carries
-- through. A person of full age and capacity: s 3(5) does not reach them (NOTHING-kind: a limit in the text's own
-- wording; others may still apply "on behalf of" a person under s 3A).
GIVEN `I may apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `I am not of full age or mental capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(5) -- the executor may apply on my behalf` `I may apply` `I am not of full age or mental capacity` MEANS
    IF `it is no` `I may apply`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `it is yes` `I may apply` AND `I am not of full age or mental capacity`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 7(a) -- the net estate`

-- s 7(a): the Court shall have regard to "the net value only of the estate of the deceased person, as ascertained by
-- deducting from the gross value thereof all debts, testamentary and funeral expenses, and all other lawful liabilities
-- to which the said estate is subject". Never below nothing (fork F5).
GIVEN `the gross value of the estate` IS A NUMBER
      `the debts` IS A NUMBER
      `the testamentary and funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER
      `the other lawful liabilities` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7(a) -- the net value of the estate` `the gross value of the estate` `the debts` `the testamentary and funeral expenses` `the other lawful liabilities` MEANS
    max 0 (`the gross value of the estate` MINUS `the deductions`)
    WHERE
        `the deductions` MEANS `the debts` PLUS `the testamentary and funeral expenses` PLUS `the other lawful liabilities`

§§ `s 9(4) -- the spouse's provision on remarriage`

-- s 9(4): "If in the opinion of the Court or a judge it is desirable so to do, ... the Court or judge may, in any order
-- under this Act making provision for the spouse of a deceased person, direct that that provision shall operate for the
-- benefit of the spouse notwithstanding that he or she may, at any time after the making of the order, remarry or enter
-- into a significant relationship". JUST TRUE where the order so directs. Where it does not, or the person is not the
-- spouse, the Act does not say what happens on remarriage: the order's own terms decide (NOTHING-kind: the text is
-- silent; fork F6).
GIVEN `I am the spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order directs that my provision continues despite remarriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(4) -- my provision continues if I remarry` `I am the spouse` `the order directs that my provision continues despite remarriage` MEANS
    IF `I am the spouse` AND `the order directs that my provision continues despite remarriage`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 9(5), (5A), (6) -- rescinding or altering an order`

-- s 9(5): "The Court or a judge may, at any time, on the application of the executor or administrator ... or of any
-- person who is beneficially entitled to, or interested in, any part of that estate -- (a) rescind any order ...; or (b)
-- alter any such order by increasing or reducing the amount of any provision". Whether I may apply: JUST TRUE for the
-- executor or administrator or a person beneficially entitled to or interested in part of the estate; otherwise NOTHING
-- (NOTHING-kind: a limit in the text's own wording, no "only").
GIVEN `I am the executor or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am beneficially entitled to or interested in part of the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(5) -- I may apply to rescind or alter the order` `I am the executor or administrator` `I am beneficially entitled to or interested in part of the estate` MEANS
    IF `I am the executor or administrator` OR `I am beneficially entitled to or interested in part of the estate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 9(6): "A person who makes an application under subsection (5) ... shall cause notice of the application to be served
-- on all persons taking any benefit under the order sought to be rescinded or altered." JUST TRUE for a person taking a
-- benefit under the order; otherwise NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent on others).
GIVEN `I take a benefit under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(6) -- I must be served with notice of the application` `I take a benefit under the order` MEANS
    IF `I take a benefit under the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 4(2) -- service of the summons`

-- s 4(2): "A summons under this section shall be served on -- (a) the executor of the will ... or the person to whom
-- letters of administration with the will annexed have been granted, or, in the case of an intestate estate, the
-- administrator of that estate; and (b) such other persons as the Court or a judge may direct". JUST TRUE for the
-- executor or administrator, or a person the Court has directed; otherwise NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent on
-- other beneficiaries; the Court may yet direct service).
GIVEN `I am the executor or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed that I be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) -- the summons must be served on me` `I am the executor or administrator` `the Court has directed that I be served` MEANS
    IF `I am the executor or administrator` OR `the Court has directed that I be served`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 10A -- who bears the provision`

-- s 10A(1): "The incidence of any payment directed to be made by an order under this Act shall, unless the Court or a
-- judge otherwise orders, fall ratably upon the whole estate of the deceased person, or, where the authority of the Court
-- does not extend ... to the whole estate, ratably upon such part of the estate as is subject to the authority of the
-- Court." (2): the Court "may exonerate any part of the estate". The part of the payment falling on my part of the
-- estate: the payment times my part's value over the value of the estate subject to the Court's authority (fork F7).
-- JUST 0 if my part is exonerated (s 10A(2)) or is outside the Court's authority. Where the Court "otherwise orders",
-- the order decides (an "unless" met: NOTHING, decided case by case, fork F8). An estate of no value: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the payment ordered` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of my part of the estate` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the estate subject to the Court's authority` IS A NUMBER
      `my part is subject to the Court's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has exonerated my part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has otherwise ordered the incidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10A -- the part of the payment falling on my part of the estate` `the payment ordered` `the value of my part of the estate` `the value of the estate subject to the Court's authority` `my part is subject to the Court's authority` `the Court has exonerated my part` `the Court has otherwise ordered the incidence` MEANS
    IF `the Court has otherwise ordered the incidence`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the Court has exonerated my part` OR (NOT `my part is subject to the Court's authority`)
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE IF `the value of the estate subject to the Court's authority` AT MOST 0
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE JUST (`the payment ordered` TIMES (`the value of my part of the estate` DIVIDED BY `the value of the estate subject to the Court's authority`))

§§ `ss 11(4), 9(5A) -- distributions already made`

-- s 11(4): "no distribution of any part of the estate made before the making of an application under that subsection
-- [an extension of time] shall be disturbed by reason of that application or of any order made thereon". s 9(5A): "The
-- Court or a judge shall not, in the exercise of the power conferred ... by paragraph (b) of subsection (5) [altering an
-- order], alter an order ... so as to disturb a distribution of any part of the estate that was lawfully made before the
-- making of the application for the alteration." Whether the distribution to me may be disturbed: JUST FALSE where a
-- flat negative protects it; otherwise NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: the text is silent -- for a claim taken out in time the Act
-- says nothing about distributions already made; fork F9).
DECLARE `The application` IS ONE OF
    `a claim taken out within the time`
    `a claim needing an extension of time`
    `an application to alter an order`

GIVEN `the application` IS A `The application`
      `the distribution to me was made before that application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distribution was lawfully made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 11(4), 9(5A) -- the distribution to me may be disturbed` `the application` `the distribution to me was made before that application` `the distribution was lawfully made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the application`
    WHEN `a claim needing an extension of time` THEN
        IF `the distribution to me was made before that application`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `an application to alter an order` THEN
        IF `the distribution to me was made before that application` AND `the distribution was lawfully made`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
